Feature: spa-style-gated-mount
Target module: SPAEngine

Problem: SPAEngine mounted every fragment with innerHTML the moment its HTML was in (cache
or network). The stylesheets the fragment carried were only requested at that point, so the
browser painted the markup unstyled until they arrived. Reported on app.myinvitees.com:
going from login to the card tool showed the header logo (an SVG with no size of its own)
filling the screen, and the tool menu unstyled, until the route's CSS loaded.

Change:
- Fragments are staged: parsed in a <template>, their top-level stylesheet links put in the
  mount point at once, then mounted in one task after those links load or fail, or after
  config.styleTimeout (default 3000ms). Links whose media doesn't match are not waited for.
- A route's content and sections mount together (flush first, then the exit callback, then
  the swap). While navigating, staged links sit behind media="not all" so the leaving route
  isn't restyled; at boot they apply as they arrive.
- Boot hides <html> (visibility) until the block sections, the entry route's sections and
  its content are mounted, so shell markup styled by fragment CSS (the logo) isn't painted
  half-styled. It is lifted on every outcome, including errors and redirects.
- With replaceOld, an identical stylesheet already in the mount point is kept, not refetched,
  when the new links' order allows.
- A navigation token supersedes stale navigations; their staged links are removed.
- Callbacks (boot, click, history) run after the styled mount.
- Fixes on the way: flush no longer blanks the header at click time; re-clicking the last
  link after back/forward reloads it; a double click on a loading link is ignored; a failed
  section is logged and skipped, not cached, and doesn't block the route.
- New: config.styleTimeout.

Verified: headless Chrome against app.myinvitees.com through a test server that delays every
stylesheet and samples each animation frame, with the original and the new engine side by side.
At 800ms per stylesheet:
  boot /card-writer: old 97 frames of unstyled menu, 57 frames of a 1369px logo; new 0 and 7
    (the 7 are the shell painted before any script runs, which vUX can't reach).
  click / -> /card-writer: old 95 frames unstyled menu, 97 unstyled content; new 0 and 0,
    the styled home page stays up until the styled tool page replaces it. Back mounts home.
At 80ms per stylesheet the new engine reaches a styled tool page at 542ms vs 410ms (boot)
and 608ms vs 551ms (click), against old pages that painted unstyled first.
vUX examples/spa: boot on /, /table, /user/7, then clicks, a repeated click, back, back,
forward and home all mount the right page, title and URL with no page errors.
Not exercised in a browser: reuse of an identical stylesheet across two routes (neither app
has a route pair that shares a links fragment).

Affected projects: app.myinvitees.com, the only app that uses SPAEngine. No API removed. Visible differences: the page is hidden
during boot until the first route is mounted, a route appears once styled instead of
progressively, and flush happens at mount time.
